[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-91
TITLE: Head Interface Communication - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the head interface board is unplugged from main control board, a fault should display in the system after 1 seconds (0.5 s for timeout
+ 0.5 s for latency)
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on, no faults present, and ready to run emission.
* Headboard communication connector on the main control board is accessible.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Use the external console to open the quality assurance tab
2. Disconnect head interface board communication connector from main control board (J601)
3. Wait for 1 second and check the system status on the top view
4. Open the error detail by pressing on the error message
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system is ready (green thumbs up icon present)
2. J601 connector is disconnected from the main control board
3. The system transitions into a “Fault” state
4. The error message indicates headboard communication timeout
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-68
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-94
TITLE: Interlocks - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware monitors and reports the status of the interlocks.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on, no faults present
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system
2. Use the external console to view the status of the interlocks (lock symbol on bottom right)
3. Activate the E-stop button on the external console
4. Activate the E-stop button on the base unit
5. Open the Door
6. Rotate the key on the external safety box to Safe
7. Remove the Collimator
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system is on
2. The interlock view is available (not gray)
3. Ensure the remote e-stop interlock is triggered
4. Ensure the remote e-stop interlock is triggered
5. Ensure the door interlock is triggered
6. Ensure the remote key interlock is triggered
7. Ensure the applicator interlock is triggered
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-8
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-98
TITLE: Operation 01: Filament conditioning 6 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware will report a fault if the conditioning process didn’t complete within 360 seconds
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on, no faults present, and ready to run emission.
* A variant that using a 1mA / 1 sec is loaded on the HVPS interface board
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system / prepare system for operation (wait for system to be “Cold” if it is in “Primed” state otherwise warmup will not run)
2. Close all interlocks and open the quality assurance tab on the external console
3. Inside “Startup Cycle” press the “Warmup” button (it runs the conditioning as the daily warmup)
4. Go to the service tab and review the Filament Feedback value under the HVPS section
5. Wait for 360 seconds
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system powers on in “Startup” state or is prepared in “Cold” or “Primed” states
2. The system is ready (green thumbs up icon present) and the “Warmup” button is available
3. Warmup begins and system transitions to “DailyWarmup” state (it is the conditioning state)
4. The Filament Feedback \[mA] value is being updated
5. The operation is not complete, and a timeout fault message is being triggered on the external console
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-12
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-99
TITLE: Operation 02: Warmup procedure - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware will report a fault if the warmup process didn’t complete within 180 seconds.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on, no faults present, and ready to run emission.
* A variant that using a 1mA / 1 sec is loaded on the HVPS interface board.
* The QC collimator is connected to the x-ray source.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system / prepare system for operation (wait for system to be “Cold” if it is in “Primed” state otherwise warmup will not run)
2. Use the external console to open the quality assurance tab
3. Open “Beam QA” and select any available energy 50/70/100kV
4. Press on “Prepare”
5. Go to the service tab and review the Filament Feedback value under the HVPS section
6. Wait for 180 seconds
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system powers on in “Startup” state or is prepared in “Cold” or “Primed” states
2. Dropdown with energies is available (at least one from 50/70/100kV)
3. At least one collimator is present in the table and “Prepare” button is enabled
4. Warmup begins and system transitions to “Warmup” state
5. The Filament Feedback \[mA] value is being updated
6. The operation is not complete, and a timeout fault message is being triggered on the external console
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-13
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-129
TITLE: Operation 05: Treatment plan release - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
If the user runs a treatment plan, its status changes from STAGED to HVPS check / HV setup.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* System is ready to run a treatment plan.
* A treatment plan is not loaded into the system.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system
2. Enter the STAGED state by loading a treatment plan
3. Toggle the door interlock, remote key interlock, and collimator interlock
4. Run the treatment plan and move ahead to the next operational state
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is started and there isn’t any plan loaded into system
2. Verify the status of the system says “STAGED” in the GUI
3. Ensure the door interlock, remote key, or collimator interlock do not trigger an interlock fault
4. Verify the states will be HV CHECK+HV SETUP after STAGED status
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-74
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-132
TITLE: Undesired emission monitoring - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware will report a fault if the emission current is higher than the max threshold of 0.2mA when not in emission.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on, no faults present, and ready to run emission.
* A variant that is reporting x10 emission current feedback is loaded on the HVPS interface board.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system
2. Check the system status
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system is on
2. The system transitions to “Fault” state with an error message about unwanted emission
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-71
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-162
TITLE: Operation 03.1: Treatment staging - new session commencement - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware will not accept a plan with more than 5 operational points and will trigger a fault.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on, no faults present, and ready to run emission.
* The QC collimator is connected to the x-ray source.
* The variant of the main control FW which attempts to load a plan with more than 5 points is loaded on the main control board.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Close all interlocks and open the quality assurance tab on the external console (wait for system to be “Cold” if it is in “Primed” state otherwise warmup will not run)
2. Use the external console to open the quality assurance tab
3. Open “Beam QA” and select any available energy 50/70/100kV
4. Press on “Prepare” and wait until warmup completes
5. The firmware variant will try to load a plan with more than 5 operational points
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system is ready (green thumbs up icon present)
2. Dropdown with energies is available (at least one from 50/70/100kV)
3. All 5 collimators are present in the table (1.5, 2, 3, 4, 5) and “Prepare” button is enabled
4. Warmup completes but high voltage is not ramping up
5. Fault message appears on the user interface on the external console and the system transitions to “Fault” state
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-40
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-170
TITLE: Operation 03.1: Treatment staging - new session commencement - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware will accept a plan with 1-5 operational points and will transition to a ready for emission state.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on, no faults present, and ready to run emission
* The QC collimator is connected to the x-ray source
* At least one energy (50/70/100) has approved physics data for all 5 collimators (1.5,2,3,4,5)
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Close all interlocks and open the quality assurance tab on the external console (wait for system to be “Cold” if it is in “Primed” state otherwise warmup will not run)
2. Use the external console to open the quality assurance tab
3. Open “Beam QA” and select any available energy 50/70/100kV
4. Press on “Prepare” and wait until warmup completes
5. Wait until high voltage completes ramp up and the system is in “Ready” state
6. Terminate the operation on the external application (no need to run emission)
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system is ready (green thumbs up icon present)
2. Dropdown with energies is available (at least one from 50/70/100kV)
3. All 5 collimators are present in the table (1.5, 2, 3, 4, 5) and “Prepare” button is enabled
4. Warmup completes and high voltage is ramping up
5. The “Ready” button is available (which means the plan was loaded successfully)
6. High voltage ramps down below 2kV and system transitions to “Primed” or “Fault” states
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-32
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-306
TITLE: QC Processing - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware receives a command from the console application, runs emission and records the accumulated values from the QC diodes
with support from the headboard
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on, no faults present, and ready to run emission.
* The QC collimator is connected to the x-ray source.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system / prepare system for operation (wait for system to be “Cold” if it is in “Primed” state otherwise warmup will not run)
2. Use the external console to open the quality assurance tab
3. Open “Beam QA” and select any available energy 50/70/100kV
4. Press on “Prepare” and wait until warmup completes
5. Wait until high voltage completes ramp up and the system is in “Ready” state
6. Press on “Beam On” (emission will start) and wait until the emission completes
7. Toggle “Reports” on the top right corner
8. Select the energy and collimator that was just tested
9. Select the latest result and review the Intensity 1 and Intensity 2 values
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system powers on in “Startup” state or is prepared in “Cold” or “Primed” states
2. Dropdown with energies is available (at least one from 50/70/100kV)
3. At least one collimator is present in the table and “Prepare” button is enabled
4. Warmup completes and high voltage is ramping up
5. The “Ready” button is available
6. Emission is ongoing and completed successfully without any interruption
7. The reports’ view appears and energy and collimator dropdowns are enabled
8. The latest QA execution matched the current time (the one just tested); results are available
9. Intensity 1 and Intensity 2 values are in the range between 26k and 806k
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-305
  ROLE: Verifies

[[/SECTION]]
